From: Adam Matthews <52178922+adamsthws@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: several peers on the air at once

The emulator held one Wi-Fi peer, which took either role: the access point
a device joins, or a station joining the device's own network. A device that
cannot join its home network raises its own while it goes on trying the
home one (ESPHome's fallback access point, OpenBeken's), so both are on the
air at once, and a test of a computer joining that network while the device
still looks for the home one needs both.

attach_wifi_peer called again now puts another peer on the air: every frame
the device sends goes to each, and each is ticked, reset with the device and
closed with the network. Each needs a MAC of its own. wifi_peer stays the
first, for callers that attach one.

A station peer takes only its own network's frames - management and data
whose BSSID is the one it joined - not the device's frames to another peer.
It takes a network silent for BEACON_LOSS_US (3 s) as gone and looks for
one again, as a real station does, so it joins the device's network again
after the device took it down and raised it once more.

set_on_air(False) takes a peer off the air: it hears nothing and sends
nothing, and forgets its links, so a device sees its access point gone, as
when a router is switched off, and joins again once it is back on.

tests/wifi_peers.py checks the two roles side by side, the loss of a
network and an access point off the air and back.
